WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.617 --> 00:00:13.290
I don't think new posters
are gonna cut it.

2
00:00:13.338 --> 00:00:14.183
What?

3
00:00:14.282 --> 00:00:16.844
You're gonna need to
up your campaign game.

4
00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:20.412
Well. perhaps my campaign
manager has some ideas.

5
00:00:20.496 --> 00:00:22.939
You mean besides
all the e-mails I sent you?

6
00:00:23.306 --> 00:00:25.059
I should
probably read those.

7
00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:27.082
Nolan.
Lopez needs a unit

8
00:00:27.166 --> 00:00:28.497
to accompany her this morning.
and that's you.

9
00:00:28.581 --> 00:00:29.559
Yes. sir.
My pleasure.

10
00:00:29.643 --> 00:00:30.762
Uh. sir...

11
00:00:30.846 --> 00:00:32.753
Can I count on your vote?

12
00:00:32.837 --> 00:00:35.681
I'm still doing my due diligence
with the candidates.

13
00:00:36.783 --> 00:00:37.888
It's Smitty!

14
00:00:37.972 --> 00:00:38.997
You got my vote.

15
00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:40.636
- Thank you.
- Not mine.

16
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.025
I'm not in
the union yet.

17
00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.361
Right.

18
00:00:49.897 --> 00:00:51.962
Looks like we're gonna be
riding together.

19
00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:54.894
Everything good?
Uh. yeah.

20
00:00:54.978 --> 00:00:57.275
We have to interview one of
these Sovereign Citizen idiots.

21
00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.387
He allegedly assaulted
an IRS agent

22
00:00:59.471 --> 00:01:01.761
who had a few questions
about why Marvin Reynolds

23
00:01:01.845 --> 00:01:03.372
wasn't paying
any of his taxes.

24
00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:05.082
Angela. I thought we were gonna
talk more this morning.

25
00:01:05.166 --> 00:01:06.019
I woke up.
you were gone.

26
00:01:06.103 --> 00:01:07.465
Yeah. I have a job.
remember?

27
00:01:07.549 --> 00:01:08.394
Uh...

28
00:01:08.478 --> 00:01:09.505
I'll wait for you
by the shop.

29
00:01:09.589 --> 00:01:11.591
I'm right behind you.

30
00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.120
Angela.

31
00:01:13.447 --> 00:01:15.512
I don't have time
for this conversation right now.

32
00:01:15.596 --> 00:01:17.712
How many times
can I apologize?

33
00:01:18.251 --> 00:01:20.566
I told you.
I didn't have a choice.

34
00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.558
Look. making a deal
with Elijah

35
00:01:22.642 --> 00:01:24.378
was the only way that I could
get you home safe.

36
00:01:24.462 --> 00:01:26.566
I understand why you did
what you did.

37
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.699
I can even understand
why you kept it from me...

38
00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:30.153
You don't want to stress out
the new mom.

39
00:01:30.237 --> 00:01:32.215
But to tell me
I need to stay out of it

40
00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:33.486
after asking
for my help...

41
00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.392
Look. I didn't
mean for you...

42
00:01:36.399 --> 00:01:38.360
I got myself into this.

43
00:01:38.444 --> 00:01:40.011
No. you got us
into this.

44
00:01:40.095 --> 00:01:41.230
and I'm going to
get us out.

45
00:01:41.314 --> 00:01:42.347
Well. how do you plan
to do that?

46
00:01:42.431 --> 00:01:44.777
By telling Elijah Stone you
don't work for him anymore.

47
00:01:44.861 --> 00:01:46.042
And if he's got
a problem with that.

48
00:01:46.126 --> 00:01:47.500
me and a couple hundred
of my closest friends...

49
00:01:47.584 --> 00:01:48.908
No. you can't.

50
00:01:49.152 --> 00:01:51.156
He has leverage on me.

51
00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.189
He could take it
to the state bar.

52
00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:54.902
I could lose
my license.

53
00:01:54.986 --> 00:01:57.672
Last night. you swore
you didn't break any laws.

54
00:01:57.756 --> 00:01:58.927
I haven't.

55
00:01:59.857 --> 00:02:02.462
There could be
some ethical questions.

56
00:02:03.401 --> 00:02:05.168
I can't do this
right now.

57
00:02:05.252 --> 00:02:07.025
We'll talk tonight.

58
00:02:10.493 --> 00:02:11.777
He can't really believe

59
00:02:11.861 --> 00:02:13.339
he can buy votes
with water bottles.

60
00:02:13.423 --> 00:02:15.348
I mean. not when I have
a real message.

61
00:02:15.432 --> 00:02:16.378
a message of change.

62
00:02:16.462 --> 00:02:18.020
Actually.
he's beating you.

63
00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.152
I did some polling.

64
00:02:19.236 --> 00:02:21.034
and you are
definitely behind.

65
00:02:21.118 --> 00:02:22.645
I'm losing to Smitty?

66
00:02:22.729 --> 00:02:24.081
Oh.
that's embarrassing.

67
00:02:24.165 --> 00:02:25.355
You know what would
really help?

68
00:02:25.439 --> 00:02:28.556
An endorsement from someone
respected within the department.

69
00:02:28.808 --> 00:02:31.159
No. don't drag me
into this.

70
00:02:31.243 --> 00:02:34.059
No. I have never endorsed
a candidate. and I never will.

71
00:02:34.143 --> 00:02:35.682
Voting is a private matter.

72
00:02:36.579 --> 00:02:39.639
Here. maybe this will help
wash away the taste of defeat.

73
00:02:39.723 --> 00:02:40.847
This bottle's
been opened.

74
00:02:40.931 --> 00:02:42.863
Oh. those bottles
are recyclable.

75
00:02:42.947 --> 00:02:44.910
It's just my way of giving back
to the environment.

76
00:02:44.994 --> 00:02:46.334
Where's the water from?

77
00:02:46.418 --> 00:02:48.072
My bathroom sink.

78
00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:49.441
Water's water.

79
00:02:49.525 --> 00:02:53.160
<i>♪ Whoa. oh. oh. oh. oh. oh.
whoa. oh. oh ♪</i>

80
00:02:53.244 --> 00:02:56.454
<i>♪ I'm gonna win for you. like I know ♪</i>
<font color=#FF00FF>*THE ROOKIE*</font>

81
00:02:56.538 --> 00:02:59.350
<i>♪ You want me to do. hey ♪</i>
<font color=#00FF00>Season 04  Episode 08</font>

82
00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:00.660
Episode Title: <font color=#FFc30f>"Hit and Run"</font>
Aired on: <font color="#00ffff">December 05. 2021.</font>

83
00:03:00.744 --> 00:03:02.673
Everything okay
with you and Wesley?

84
00:03:02.885 --> 00:03:04.433
- No.
- I get it.

85
00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.868
Sarah wanted to divorce me
at least three times

86
00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:08.668
during Henry's
first year.

87
00:03:08.752 --> 00:03:10.370
It felt like I couldn't
get anything right.

88
00:03:10.454 --> 00:03:11.886
It's rough.
those early days.

89
00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.894
You know. it's a lack of sleep.
it's fear of the unknown.

90
00:03:14.978 --> 00:03:16.328
a baby that
won't stop crying...

91
00:03:16.412 --> 00:03:17.907
It's not about that.

92
00:03:17.991 --> 00:03:19.447
What is it about?

93
00:03:20.213 --> 00:03:22.464
Right now. it's about you
not minding your own business.

94
00:03:22.548 --> 00:03:24.413
Put the shop in drive
and let's go.

95
00:03:24.497 --> 00:03:25.781
I will have to
put it in reverse

96
00:03:25.865 --> 00:03:27.523
before I can
actually put it...

97
00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.842
I know that look.
No more jokes.

98
00:03:36.023 --> 00:03:37.132
Genny.

99
00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:38.881
Sergeant Bradford.

100
00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:41.918
You look skinny.

101
00:03:42.002 --> 00:03:43.040
Have you been eating?

102
00:03:43.124 --> 00:03:44.617
- Every day.
- Uh-huh.

103
00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:46.289
This is a restricted area.
How'd you get in here?

104
00:03:46.373 --> 00:03:48.621
Oh. the guy who's
handing out waters let me in.

105
00:03:48.705 --> 00:03:51.110
Okay. Yeah.
Don't drink that.

106
00:03:51.194 --> 00:03:52.553
Um...

107
00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:53.855
So. what are you
doing here?

108
00:03:53.939 --> 00:03:56.237
I just wanted to
see my big brother.

109
00:03:56.321 --> 00:03:58.711
Oh. hi.
I'm Lucy Chen.

110
00:03:58.795 --> 00:03:59.664
I know that
we just met.

111
00:03:59.748 --> 00:04:01.142
but if you have
any embarrassing stories

112
00:04:01.226 --> 00:04:03.110
from his childhood.
that...

113
00:04:06.107 --> 00:04:07.459
So you just
wanted to see me?

114
00:04:07.543 --> 00:04:09.353
I didn't even know
you were in town.

115
00:04:09.437 --> 00:04:10.813
So you're not just not
returning my calls.

116
00:04:10.897 --> 00:04:11.883
you're also ignoring
the messages

117
00:04:11.967 --> 00:04:12.945
telling you
I'm coming to town.

118
00:04:13.029 --> 00:04:14.257
Because I know
why you're here.

119
00:04:14.341 --> 00:04:16.701
and I've made
my position very clear.

120
00:04:17.684 --> 00:04:19.373
We have to
talk about it.

121
00:04:20.202 --> 00:04:21.452
Look. I gotta
get to work.

122
00:04:21.537 --> 00:04:23.678
Maybe we can
have dinner tonight.

123
00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.928
So you can
blow me off at the last minute?

124
00:04:26.226 --> 00:04:27.578
No.

125
00:04:27.662 --> 00:04:30.843
Why don't I do one of those
ride-along thingies?

126
00:04:30.927 --> 00:04:32.907
That way. we could have
the whole day to catch up.

127
00:04:32.991 --> 00:04:33.899
Yeah.

128
00:04:33.983 --> 00:04:35.633
See. you gotta get permission
to do a ride-along.

129
00:04:35.717 --> 00:04:36.727
It's...

130
00:04:36.811 --> 00:04:38.618
It's a long process.
a ton of paperwork.

131
00:04:38.702 --> 00:04:39.548
Hey. you're
a sergeant now.

132
00:04:39.632 --> 00:04:41.251
You can just
approve it yourself.

133
00:04:41.335 --> 00:04:42.579
Great.

134
00:04:42.663 --> 00:04:44.360
Let's hit the streets.

135
00:04:44.444 --> 00:04:45.858
Let's.

136
00:04:47.449 --> 00:04:48.958
Did Tim have any. um.

137
00:04:49.042 --> 00:04:50.889
nicknames
when he was a kid?

138
00:04:57.516 --> 00:05:00.210
So. it's been
six weeks.

139
00:05:00.319 --> 00:05:02.303
Any thoughts
on my progress?

140
00:05:02.387 --> 00:05:04.228
I write an evaluation
every day.

141
00:05:04.312 --> 00:05:06.899
Those are my thoughts
on your progress.

142
00:05:06.983 --> 00:05:08.585
Right. I mean.
that's the technical stuff.

143
00:05:08.669 --> 00:05:10.234
but I was just
wondering. like.

144
00:05:10.318 --> 00:05:12.295
what you thought of me
as a person.

145
00:05:13.235 --> 00:05:15.672
What matters is what
I think about you as a cop.

146
00:05:15.756 --> 00:05:19.412
You want people to like you.
go make some friends.

147
00:05:23.985 --> 00:05:25.375
Harper.

148
00:05:27.194 --> 00:05:28.576
What?

149
00:05:29.282 --> 00:05:30.211
Oh. no. no.

150
00:05:30.295 --> 00:05:32.047
This is the first
I'm hearing about this.

151
00:05:32.615 --> 00:05:34.990
He can't do that.
though. right?

152
00:05:37.016 --> 00:05:38.649
Maybe?
W-What do you mean maybe?

153
00:05:38.733 --> 00:05:39.869
You...
You are the lawyer.

154
00:05:39.953 --> 00:05:41.842
Shouldn't you know that
for sure?

155
00:05:41.948 --> 00:05:43.133
Okay. well.
I-I'ma need you

156
00:05:43.217 --> 00:05:45.389
to get some damn clarity
and call me back.

157
00:05:47.987 --> 00:05:49.748
- Is everything okay?
- No.

158
00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:54.216
My ex-husband
is getting married.

159
00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.238
and he wants to move
to San Francisco

160
00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.139
and take my daughter
with him.

161
00:05:58.949 --> 00:06:00.451
Can he do that?

162
00:06:00.889 --> 00:06:02.162
I don't know.

163
00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:05.693
This is Detective Angela Lopez.
badge number 1777.

164
00:06:05.777 --> 00:06:08.741
I need complete histories.
statewide and CJIC.

165
00:06:08.825 --> 00:06:10.237
for the personal
file numbers...

166
00:06:10.321 --> 00:06:15.695
NWC-057. JPA-733.
BXR-389.

167
00:06:15.779 --> 00:06:18.204
And if any of those queries
generate other file numbers.

168
00:06:18.288 --> 00:06:19.703
can I get completes
on those. too?

169
00:06:19.787 --> 00:06:21.041
Thanks.

170
00:06:22.456 --> 00:06:23.993
What was that about?

171
00:06:24.077 --> 00:06:25.821
Uh. another case
I'm working on.

172
00:06:25.905 --> 00:06:27.283
Anything
I can help with?

173
00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:29.377
No. I got it handled.

174
00:06:29.461 --> 00:06:32.219
Oh. yeah. he tried to highlight
his hair right before prom.

175
00:06:32.303 --> 00:06:33.947
He ended up
looking like Slim Shady.

176
00:06:34.031 --> 00:06:35.341
Hm!
Oh. you know what?

177
00:06:35.425 --> 00:06:36.753
I think I have a picture of it.

178
00:06:36.837 --> 00:06:38.970
- Oh. my God. yes!
- Genny.

179
00:06:39.054 --> 00:06:41.280
What. you'd... you'd rather
I keep this photo private?

180
00:06:41.364 --> 00:06:44.008
That's fine.
Let's talk about dad.

181
00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:46.117
I have nothing to say.

182
00:06:46.234 --> 00:06:47.343
Okay.

183
00:06:47.428 --> 00:06:49.243
What's your cellphone number?
I'll text it to you.

184
00:06:49.328 --> 00:06:51.635
Genny. come on.
We don't need your distractions.

185
00:06:51.719 --> 00:06:53.430
Police work
is serious stuff.

186
00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:58.641
Ooh. boy.

