You'll never catch me!

190
00:07:15.781 --> 00:07:17.355
Have you been
drinking?

191
00:07:17.439 --> 00:07:20.457
It's not illegal
to drink and bike.

192
00:07:20.541 --> 00:07:21.937
Actually. it is.

193
00:07:22.021 --> 00:07:24.316
The way you were swerving
in and out of traffic...

194
00:07:24.403 --> 00:07:25.631
Oh. Uh...

195
00:07:25.715 --> 00:07:27.490
You could have caused
an accident.

196
00:07:27.574 --> 00:07:30.495
- Alright?
- I just wanna get some tacos!

197
00:07:30.602 --> 00:07:33.115
Don't be such a butt.

198
00:07:33.199 --> 00:07:35.428
Okay. ma'am. we can cite you
for public intoxication.

199
00:07:35.512 --> 00:07:38.413
or if you don't cooperate.
we'll charge you with a DUI.

200
00:07:38.497 --> 00:07:43.682
Screw you. you
Ken-doll-ass-looking mimbo...

201
00:07:43.766 --> 00:07:44.803
Hey. honey.

202
00:07:44.887 --> 00:07:46.170
Honey. I know
you're having a bad day.

203
00:07:46.254 --> 00:07:47.624
but that doesn't give you
the right to be rude.

204
00:07:47.708 --> 00:07:49.262
They're just doing
their jobs.

205
00:07:49.603 --> 00:07:51.128
Why don't you take
a few deep breaths

206
00:07:51.212 --> 00:07:52.808
and sit down
for a minute?

207
00:07:54.993 --> 00:07:56.535
I'm sorry.

208
00:07:59.947 --> 00:08:01.295
That was impressive.

209
00:08:01.379 --> 00:08:03.205
I teach
fourth graders.

210
00:08:07.183 --> 00:08:08.654
Oh. great.

211
00:08:08.738 --> 00:08:12.045
Okay. look. you cannot move
our daughter to San Francisco.

212
00:08:12.129 --> 00:08:13.265
What... What...
What are we gonna do?

213
00:08:13.349 --> 00:08:15.453
Put her on a plane
every weekend?

214
00:08:15.537 --> 00:08:16.497
Enroll her
in two schools?

215
00:08:16.581 --> 00:08:17.881
No. obviously not.

216
00:08:17.965 --> 00:08:20.139
What you are asking for
is near total custody

217
00:08:20.223 --> 00:08:22.170
and I see her on weekends
and holidays. which...

218
00:08:22.254 --> 00:08:25.825
Which is a violation of our
custody agreement. by the way.

219
00:08:25.909 --> 00:08:27.646
- so I...
- I'm gonna need...

220
00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.091
<i>If you're satisfied with
your message. press one.</i>

221
00:08:30.175 --> 00:08:32.144
<i>If you'd like to
re-record. pre...</i>

222
00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:36.037
Look. I know he's
your daughter's father.

223
00:08:36.121 --> 00:08:38.832
but that man is a coward
for springing this on you.

224
00:08:40.503 --> 00:08:44.560
Well. he might have
left a message last week

225
00:08:44.644 --> 00:08:47.345
saying that he needed to talk
to me about something. but...

226
00:08:47.429 --> 00:08:49.513
Maybe it was two messages.

227
00:08:49.597 --> 00:08:52.861
There might have been
an e-mail. But...

228
00:08:53.043 --> 00:08:54.622
Okay. Then. why didn't you
call him back?

229
00:08:54.706 --> 00:08:56.798
I don't know. I thought
it was about something else.

230
00:08:56.882 --> 00:08:58.191
Oh. so you were
avoiding him?

231
00:08:58.275 --> 00:09:00.108
No. I was n...

232
00:09:00.201 --> 00:09:01.741
I don't know. Maybe.

233
00:09:02.461 --> 00:09:05.053
I did... I didn't want to
have to talk about...

234
00:09:05.335 --> 00:09:06.963
Halloween.

235
00:09:07.763 --> 00:09:09.366
What happened
on Halloween?

236
00:09:11.288 --> 00:09:12.897
Ohhh.
Mm.

237
00:09:14.015 --> 00:09:14.938
Sorry.

238
00:09:15.022 --> 00:09:17.345
Well. we're about to land
at Marvin Reynolds' place.

239
00:09:17.429 --> 00:09:18.603
What are we
hoping for?

240
00:09:18.687 --> 00:09:20.518
Ideally. he admits to
assaulting the IRS agent

241
00:09:20.602 --> 00:09:21.606
and we hook him up.

242
00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.129
Otherwise. it's just
a misdemeanor

243
00:09:23.213 --> 00:09:25.479
not committed
in police presence.

244
00:09:25.563 --> 00:09:27.946
His word against
the IRS agent's.

245
00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:29.731
Yeah. I always mix up these
Sovereign Citizen guys

246
00:09:29.815 --> 00:09:32.514
with the
Posse Comitatus group.

247
00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:33.821
They're all just part of

248
00:09:33.905 --> 00:09:36.054
the same crazy.
anti-government soup...

249
00:09:36.283 --> 00:09:39.499
All just looking for their way
not to pay their fair share.

250
00:09:39.621 --> 00:09:41.277
I think there's a little
more to it than that.

251
00:09:41.361 --> 00:09:42.975
Good for you.

252
00:09:43.059 --> 00:09:44.562
Look. there's always
people in society

253
00:09:44.646 --> 00:09:46.672
who feel like
they're on the outside.

254
00:09:46.756 --> 00:09:48.936
And some are
easily manipulated.

255
00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.549
Some are so desperate
to find a purpose

256
00:09:51.633 --> 00:09:53.398
that they allow themselves
to be infected

257
00:09:53.482 --> 00:09:54.922
by the most absurd
beliefs.

258
00:09:55.006 --> 00:09:56.704
so much so.
they could rationalize

259
00:09:57.006 --> 00:09:58.382
beating up
an IRS agent...

260
00:09:58.466 --> 00:09:59.787
Or worse.

261
00:09:59.871 --> 00:10:02.007
Nah.
My theory's better.

262
00:10:02.091 --> 00:10:04.203
These whack jobs just believe
they're above the law.

263
00:10:04.287 --> 00:10:05.779
until they need it.

264
00:10:07.458 --> 00:10:08.807
There it is.

265
00:10:21.445 --> 00:10:22.710
This guy have
a history of violence?

266
00:10:22.794 --> 00:10:25.017
Why do you think
I'm putting on a vest?

267
00:10:25.101 --> 00:10:27.933
Let me guess.
Domestic abuse?

268
00:10:28.017 --> 00:10:30.190
Among other things.
but he never did any time.

269
00:10:37.234 --> 00:10:39.455
Hey. get the hell off
of my property!

270
00:10:39.539 --> 00:10:42.241
Sir. I'm Detective Lopez.
and this is Officer Nolan.

271
00:10:42.325 --> 00:10:43.548
Are you
Marvin Reynolds?

272
00:10:43.632 --> 00:10:45.377
You know what?
That name is a straw-man. okay?

273
00:10:45.461 --> 00:10:47.585
I'm a free man.
I'm living upon the land.

274
00:10:47.669 --> 00:10:49.421
You're representatives of
a corporate government.

275
00:10:49.505 --> 00:10:51.032
You have no authority
over me.

276
00:10:51.116 --> 00:10:53.885
I am not a citizen of
your corporation!

277
00:10:53.969 --> 00:10:55.965
Sir. a complaint's been
filed against you

278
00:10:56.049 --> 00:10:58.316
claiming you assaulted
a federal employee from the IRS.

279
00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.167
Yeah. they're trying to
take my house.

280
00:11:00.251 --> 00:11:01.674
Okay?
But. see. there's no

281
00:11:01.758 --> 00:11:02.799
legitimate money.

282
00:11:02.883 --> 00:11:05.237
because we went off
the gold standard in 1933.

283
00:11:05.321 --> 00:11:07.277
So you're admitting
to the assault?

284
00:11:08.397 --> 00:11:10.188
No. I admit nothing. okay?

285
00:11:10.272 --> 00:11:12.284
And I don't... I don't...
I don't have any obligation

286
00:11:12.368 --> 00:11:14.041
to submit
to your unlawful inquiry.

287
00:11:14.125 --> 00:11:15.917
Sir. we need to talk to you
about what happened.

288
00:11:16.001 --> 00:11:17.612
Can you please step out
onto the porch?

289
00:11:17.696 --> 00:11:20.028
I'm a constitutional activist.
okay?

290
00:11:20.112 --> 00:11:21.564
I know my rights.

291
00:11:21.648 --> 00:11:24.350
A-A-And what you're
practicing here. it's tyranny.

292
00:11:24.434 --> 00:11:26.992
Sir. we just want
your side of the story.

293
00:11:27.076 --> 00:11:29.159
I promise you. this will be
much more productive

294
00:11:29.243 --> 00:11:30.893
if you just step out
onto the porch.

295
00:11:30.977 --> 00:11:32.258
Ah.

296
00:11:32.342 --> 00:11:35.041
Yeah. that's...
That's not gonna happen.

297
00:11:35.125 --> 00:11:36.049
Okay?

298
00:11:36.133 --> 00:11:40.000
So get off of my property.
Now.

299
00:11:40.742 --> 00:11:43.797
Sir. take it easy.

300
00:11:43.881 --> 00:11:45.664
Don't do anything stupid.

301
00:11:47.904 --> 00:11:49.884
Sir?

302
00:11:49.968 --> 00:11:51.578
Gun!
Move. move. move!

303
00:11:54.843 --> 00:11:56.331
7-Adam-15.

304
00:11:56.415 --> 00:11:58.947
Shots fired at our location.
Send backup. Code 3.

305
00:11:59.031 --> 00:12:01.598
You ready?
Yeah.

306
00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.567
He's going outside.
He's running.

307
00:12:23.001 --> 00:12:25.134
No!

308
00:12:29.399 --> 00:12:31.360
Control. 7-Adam-15.
Code 3 traffic.

309
00:12:31.444 --> 00:12:33.908
We just got 246'd
by a submachine gun.

310
00:12:33.992 --> 00:12:35.843
Suspect vehicle...
Silver sedan.

311
00:12:35.927 --> 00:12:37.497
last seen headed west
on Oakwood.

312
00:12:37.581 --> 00:12:39.178
Suspect still armed.

313
00:12:42.811 --> 00:12:44.073
Air Three
is lifting now.

314
00:12:44.158 --> 00:12:46.612
I'm ten-nine-seven.
Searching for suspect's vehicle.

315
00:12:48.769 --> 00:12:51.135
Control. 7-Adam-100
on scene.

316
00:12:54.249 --> 00:12:56.066
Stay in the car.

317
00:12:56.251 --> 00:12:57.322
Anybody hurt?

318
00:12:57.538 --> 00:12:59.762
We're good. but we've got
one shooter outstanding...

319
00:12:59.847 --> 00:13:00.870
Marvin Reynolds.

320
00:13:00.955 --> 00:13:02.371
Suspect vehicle...
Silver sedan.

321
00:13:02.456 --> 00:13:04.355
Did not get very good I.D.
I didn't get any plates.

322
00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:05.535
Alright. let's pull
DMV records.

323
00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:06.917
see what Marvin's
got registered.

324
00:13:07.002 --> 00:13:08.331
Got to find everything
we can about this guy.

325
00:13:08.416 --> 00:13:09.238
- On it.
- I'll ask for

326
00:13:09.323 --> 00:13:10.082
a telephonic warrant

327
00:13:10.183 --> 00:13:11.824
to search the GPS of
his vehicle on his phone.

328
00:13:11.863 --> 00:13:12.857
If we can see where he's been.

329
00:13:12.941 --> 00:13:14.247
it might help us know
where he's going.

330
00:13:14.332 --> 00:13:15.881
Control. 7-Adam-100.
advise crime scene

331
00:13:15.965 --> 00:13:17.631
they can begin processing
and start a board-up crew.

332
00:13:17.715 --> 00:13:20.013
And I need all available units
for a city-wide manhunt.

333
00:13:20.097 --> 00:13:22.998
Alright. listen up...
At approximately 1057 hours.

334
00:13:23.082 --> 00:13:24.615
suspect Marvin Reynolds
opened fire

335
00:13:24.699 --> 00:13:26.131
on Officer Nolan
and Detective Lopez

336
00:13:26.215 --> 00:13:27.193
with a submachine gun.

337
00:13:27.277 --> 00:13:28.543
We're dealing with
a Sovereign Citizen

338
00:13:28.627 --> 00:13:29.529
who's clearly snapped.

339
00:13:29.613 --> 00:13:32.100
He assaulted an IRS agent
who showed up two days ago

340
00:13:32.184 --> 00:13:33.482
to start foreclosure
proceedings.

341
00:13:33.566 --> 00:13:35.271
We're gonna hit up
every known address.

342
00:13:35.355 --> 00:13:37.456
every relative's address.
every associate.

343
00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:39.006
every friend of a friend
of a friend

344
00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:40.482
until someone
coughs this guy up.

345
00:13:40.566 --> 00:13:43.115
Okay. he hasn't renewed any of
his registrations in over four years.

346
00:13:43.199 --> 00:13:45.427
but I got a list of everything
he's owned going back to 2005.

347
00:13:45.511 --> 00:13:47.201
You got a silver Honda
on there or a Toyota?

348
00:13:47.285 --> 00:13:49.073
There's a silver Civic.
as well as three other vehicles.

349
00:13:49.157 --> 00:13:50.341
Alright. send that list
to everyone's boxes.

350
00:13:50.425 --> 00:13:51.357
Make sure
you keep checking.

351
00:13:51.441 --> 00:13:53.155
This is a very fluid
situation.

352
00:13:53.239 --> 00:13:55.577
Now let's go get this guy
before he does something worse.

353
00:13:55.661 --> 00:13:56.763
Phew.

354
00:13:56.847 --> 00:13:57.834
What's going on?

355
00:13:57.918 --> 00:13:59.756
I'm taking you back to the station.
It's too dangerous.

356
00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:01.139
- Forget it.
- Genny.

357
00:14:01.223 --> 00:14:03.569
I'm not leaving until
we talk about dad.

358
00:14:03.653 --> 00:14:04.921
Oh. you are impossible.

359
00:14:05.005 --> 00:14:06.222
I'm impossible?

360
00:14:06.467 --> 00:14:08.102
Lucy. who's more difficult.
me or Tim?

361
00:14:08.186 --> 00:14:09.701
Of course
she's gonna pick me!

362
00:14:09.785 --> 00:14:11.468
Because you are the most
stubborn person alive.

363
00:14:11.552 --> 00:14:12.868
which is. by the way.
why you're still single.

364
00:14:12.952 --> 00:14:14.878
Okay.
First of all. I'm not.

365
00:14:14.962 --> 00:14:16.204
- And second...
- Wait. What?

366
00:14:16.288 --> 00:14:18.188
- You're seeing someone?
- This is insane.

367
00:14:18.272 --> 00:14:20.336
There is an armed and dangerous
suspect at large.

368
00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:22.147
We gotta focus.

369
00:14:29.462 --> 00:14:30.626
Are you okay?

370
00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:32.251
I'm fine.
I've been shot at before.

371
00:14:32.335 --> 00:14:34.032
That's not what
I'm talking about.

372
00:14:34.116 --> 00:14:35.477
Something else
is going on here.

373
00:14:35.561 --> 00:14:38.546
and maybe a friendly ear
will help.

374
00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.678
Wesley made a deal
with Elijah Stone

375
00:14:42.762 --> 00:14:45.084
to find out where La Fiera
was keeping me in Guatemala.

376
00:14:45.168 --> 00:14:47.820
and now Elijah is
threatening our family.

377
00:14:50.623 --> 00:14:52.022
What do we do?

378
00:14:53.257 --> 00:14:55.102
Thank you. but I'm trying to
figure that out.

379
00:14:55.186 --> 00:14:56.681
Well. it doesn't seem
that complicated.

380
00:14:56.765 --> 00:14:59.006
He's a criminal.
and you're a cop.

381
00:14:59.191 --> 00:15:02.586
There's an element I can't talk about.
but it muddies things.

382
00:15:03.125 --> 00:15:06.196
Well. for what it's worth.

383
00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:09.032
I have never met a couple
so different from each other

384
00:15:09.116 --> 00:15:11.681
and yet so perfect
for one another.

385
00:15:11.765 --> 00:15:13.454
I can't imagine what it is
you're facing.

386
00:15:13.538 --> 00:15:15.321
but I do know this...

387
00:15:15.405 --> 00:15:18.144
The only way you're gonna
get through it is together.

388
00:15:22.092 --> 00:15:23.692
Pull over.

389
00:15:23.776 --> 00:15:24.860
You gonna throw up?

390
00:15:24.944 --> 00:15:26.069
Was that a little
too saccharine?

391
00:15:26.153 --> 00:15:27.772
A little.
but I need to make a call.

392
00:15:27.856 --> 00:15:29.772
I've been known to
keep a secret.

393
00:15:29.856 --> 00:15:31.327
I need to make a call.

394
00:15:31.411 --> 00:15:32.851
and unless you want to
be subpoenaed one day.

395
00:15:32.935 --> 00:15:34.704
you can't hear any of it.
so pull over.

396
00:15:34.788 --> 00:15:36.028
Roger that.

397
00:15:48.686 --> 00:15:50.387
Hey. it's me.

398
00:15:50.471 --> 00:15:51.569
Hey.
Are we okay?

399
00:15:51.653 --> 00:15:52.721
I'm working on it.

400
00:15:52.805 --> 00:15:54.100
I've been digging
into everything

401
00:15:54.184 --> 00:15:55.608
I can find about Elijah.

402
00:15:55.692 --> 00:15:56.987
and I think I have a plan.

403
00:15:57.071 --> 00:15:59.207
We're going to build
a RICO case against him

404
00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:01.319
and make sure
he rots in jail.

405
00:16:01.403 --> 00:16:03.874
which means I need you to
document every interaction

406
00:16:03.958 --> 00:16:05.256
you've ever had
with Elijah...

407
00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:07.186
Every threat
or implied threat.

408
00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.749
admission
to his own crimes

409
00:16:08.833 --> 00:16:10.435
or the crimes of
his criminal enterprise.

410
00:16:10.519 --> 00:16:11.803
No. I can't.

411
00:16:11.887 --> 00:16:13.675
That violates
attorney-client privilege.

412
00:16:13.759 --> 00:16:15.460
- Are you serious?
- I know.

413
00:16:15.544 --> 00:16:17.594
He threatened
your wife and baby.

414
00:16:17.678 --> 00:16:19.600
The privilege belongs
to the client.

415
00:16:19.684 --> 00:16:20.922
It's not my privilege
to waive.

416
00:16:21.006 --> 00:16:22.484
You made a vow.

417
00:16:22.568 --> 00:16:23.747
What's more important.

418
00:16:23.831 --> 00:16:25.789
your vow to your client
or to me?

419
00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:30.623
Oh. up on the right...
Silver one.

420
00:16:30.707 --> 00:16:32.794
No. wrong make
and model.

421
00:16:33.613 --> 00:16:36.244
Any other plans
while you're in L.A.?

422
00:16:36.328 --> 00:16:38.559
I have to sell our dad's house.

423
00:16:38.654 --> 00:16:40.225
He hasn't been able to live
on his own for awhile.

424
00:16:40.309 --> 00:16:42.138
Oh. I'm sorry.

425
00:16:42.222 --> 00:16:44.620
Thanks. It's a mess.

426
00:16:44.704 --> 00:16:46.123
It's a lot of work
for one person.

427
00:16:46.207 --> 00:16:47.655
Well. I'm sure
Tim will help.

428
00:16:47.739 --> 00:16:49.006
- What's the point?
- It's a teardown.

429
00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:51.009
Just sell it
and be done with it.

430
00:16:51.093 --> 00:16:52.084
It's got good bones.

431
00:16:52.168 --> 00:16:53.874
We could make some money
if we put in a little effort.

432
00:16:53.958 --> 00:16:56.607
You watch a couple hours of HGTV
and now you're an expert?

433
00:16:56.691 --> 00:16:58.350
Wait. what is
your favorite show?

434
00:16:58.434 --> 00:16:59.875
Mine is "House Hunters
International."

435
00:16:59.959 --> 00:17:01.796
Oh. my God. The best.

436
00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:04.013
Nolan. can you 10-3
to another channel?

437
00:17:04.184 --> 00:17:05.413
Roger that.
Going to 6.

438
00:17:05.497 --> 00:17:07.600
Yeah. look. my sister needs
to sell my dad's house.

439
00:17:07.684 --> 00:17:09.277
but it hasn't been
updated or repaired

440
00:17:09.361 --> 00:17:10.780
since it was built
in 1958.

441
00:17:10.864 --> 00:17:12.593
What are the inspections
gonna reveal?

442
00:17:12.677 --> 00:17:14.280
Uh. 1958?

443
00:17:14.364 --> 00:17:16.574
It's probably got old
cloth-insulated wiring

444
00:17:16.658 --> 00:17:17.905
that would need to
be replaced.

445
00:17:17.989 --> 00:17:20.092
Uh. the plumbing would
need to be updated.

446
00:17:20.176 --> 00:17:22.095
The cast-iron sewer
could be cracked

447
00:17:22.179 --> 00:17:23.342
or rusted through
in places.

448
00:17:23.426 --> 00:17:25.084
and the foundations
would need to be checked.

449
00:17:25.168 --> 00:17:26.530
So it's a teardown.

450
00:17:26.614 --> 00:17:27.947
Oh. no.
not necessarily.

451
00:17:28.031 --> 00:17:28.928
If it has good bones.

452
00:17:29.012 --> 00:17:30.472
some simple repairs
and updates

453
00:17:30.556 --> 00:17:32.241
would double the value
of your house.

454
00:17:32.325 --> 00:17:34.031
I'm happy to swing by.
take a look at it.

455
00:17:34.115 --> 00:17:34.983
see what needs
to be done.

456
00:17:35.067 --> 00:17:37.117
Alright. you will all
have to wait your turn.

457
00:17:37.201 --> 00:17:41.445
Nolan is busy helping me install
my new kitchen backsplash.

458
00:17:41.529 --> 00:17:42.969
Right. but after that.

459
00:17:43.053 --> 00:17:44.233
Kind of regretting
telling everyone

460
00:17:44.317 --> 00:17:45.888
you used to be a contractor.
aren't you?

461
00:17:45.972 --> 00:17:47.586
Hey. Nolan.
do you do pergolas?

462
00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.702
'Cause my outdoor space
is really underused.

463
00:17:49.786 --> 00:17:52.084
Landscaping's not really
my area of expertise.

464
00:17:52.168 --> 00:17:54.148
but I have built
a gazebo or two in my day.

465
00:17:54.232 --> 00:17:56.193
Hold on. We just
got sent a location

466
00:17:56.277 --> 00:17:58.369
of one of Marvin Reynolds'
vehicles.

467
00:17:58.453 --> 00:18:00.023
Looks like he's got an RV

468
00:18:00.107 --> 00:18:01.503
that's been collecting
parking tickets

469
00:18:01.587 --> 00:18:03.475
on the 1600 block
of Crenshaw.

470
00:18:03.559 --> 00:18:04.983
We're closest.
We'll... We'll take it.

471
00:18:05.067 --> 00:18:06.926
Heading there now.

472
00:18:13.316 --> 00:18:14.488
Is that from
your lawyer?

473
00:18:14.572 --> 00:18:15.637
Uh. yeah.

474
00:18:15.721 --> 00:18:17.823
It's about
three pages of legalese

475
00:18:17.907 --> 00:18:20.418
that basically comes down to.
I am screwed.

476
00:18:20.502 --> 00:18:21.520
Yeah. but
you're the mom.

477
00:18:21.604 --> 00:18:22.996
I mean.
that has to matter.

478
00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.238
Yeah. I'm the mom who all
but abandoned her daughter

479
00:18:25.322 --> 00:18:27.512
when I went undercover
and then nearly got her killed.

480
00:18:27.596 --> 00:18:29.504
Donovan is the one
who was there for her.

481
00:18:29.588 --> 00:18:30.848
Okay. but that
was the past.

482
00:18:30.932 --> 00:18:33.184
Look. I've seen you.
okay?

483
00:18:33.268 --> 00:18:34.598
You're a great mom.

484
00:18:34.682 --> 00:18:37.270
Would a great mom put her kid
through a second custody battle?

485
00:18:37.354 --> 00:18:39.152
I mean. last time
was a nightmare.

486
00:18:39.236 --> 00:18:42.027
She had trouble sleeping.
Her school work suffered.

487
00:18:42.111 --> 00:18:44.323
I just... I don't know
if I can do that again.

488
00:18:44.407 --> 00:18:45.988
- There's our RV.
- Alright.

489
00:18:46.072 --> 00:18:48.111
Be ready to bail in case
he opens fire on us.

490
00:18:48.195 --> 00:18:49.366
Got that.

491
00:19:14.007 --> 00:19:15.273
Yeah. VIN matches.

492
00:19:15.357 --> 00:19:17.103
This is our guy's.

493
00:19:17.187 --> 00:19:20.000
Looks abandoned. but it don't
mean he ain't held up inside.

494
00:19:22.753 --> 00:19:24.228
Alright.
What's the play. Boot?

495
00:19:24.312 --> 00:19:25.970
Well. there's only
one entry point.

496
00:19:26.054 --> 00:19:28.688
so we stay safe
and. uh. try to see

497
00:19:28.772 --> 00:19:30.169
if we can get him to come out
with verbal commands.

498
00:19:30.253 --> 00:19:32.164
And if there's
no response?

499
00:19:32.738 --> 00:19:33.868
Breach?

500
00:19:33.952 --> 00:19:35.432
Or...

501
00:19:44.129 --> 00:19:45.228
Ball-Cam.

502
00:19:45.312 --> 00:19:48.287
360-degree view.
It can even swim.

503
00:19:48.371 --> 00:19:51.368
I am in no mood to play games
with this guy.

504
00:19:51.452 --> 00:19:53.265
We just have to
get it inside.

505
00:20:14.845 --> 00:20:16.334
Man.

506
00:20:16.418 --> 00:20:18.685
This guy
is ready for war.

507
00:20:18.769 --> 00:20:20.775
- So. are we going in?
- Hold on. One sec.

508
00:20:20.859 --> 00:20:21.674
I gotta
check the door.

509
00:20:21.758 --> 00:20:23.697
make sure it's not rigged
with explosives.

510
00:20:23.781 --> 00:20:25.821
Yeah. he definitely
seems like the type.

511
00:20:25.905 --> 00:20:27.478
Alright.
I don't see any wires.

512
00:20:27.562 --> 00:20:29.328
We're all clear.

513
00:20:44.984 --> 00:20:46.860
Alright.
We're all clear.

514
00:20:46.944 --> 00:20:49.627
Control. 7-Adam-07.
we're code 4.

515
00:20:49.711 --> 00:20:51.040
RV is unoccupied.

516
00:20:51.703 --> 00:20:54.536
"Rebirth through
the blood of innocents."

517
00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.227
Looks like we got ourselves
a manifesto.

518
00:21:00.105 --> 00:21:03.334
Control. Air Three is moving
over to the northeast grid.

519
00:21:03.459 --> 00:21:04.982
<i>Copy. Air Three.</i>

520
00:21:06.977 --> 00:21:08.024
Listen to this...

521
00:21:08.108 --> 00:21:12.573
"Satanic-Hebrew Anglo-Commerce
devoured America."

522
00:21:12.657 --> 00:21:14.619
"The Cabal's slaves
have vanquished us.

523
00:21:14.703 --> 00:21:16.533
Your blood flows
gutter-rivers today."

524
00:21:16.617 --> 00:21:18.385
"The time is at hand
for renewal.

525
00:21:18.469 --> 00:21:20.650
and we will use
the blood of the masters

526
00:21:20.734 --> 00:21:23.478
to wash away
the incestuous sins

527
00:21:23.562 --> 00:21:25.877
of the corrupt
adjudicators."

528
00:21:25.961 --> 00:21:28.262
Barely literate
and yet truly terrifying.

529
00:21:28.346 --> 00:21:30.786
The good news is. we found
the RV with his stash of guns

530
00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:31.961
before he could
get to them.

531
00:21:32.045 --> 00:21:33.528
Even if all he has
is a submachine gun.

532
00:21:33.612 --> 00:21:35.885
we're still looking at a
potential mass-casualty event.

533
00:21:35.969 --> 00:21:37.579
He post anything
to social media?

534
00:21:37.663 --> 00:21:40.844
Nothing new. A dozen older
posts. tilting at windmills.

535
00:21:40.928 --> 00:21:42.850
But he's only got
like 10 followers.

536
00:21:42.934 --> 00:21:44.810
Not sure how wide
his message spread.

537
00:21:44.894 --> 00:21:47.041
Maybe he's using a secret
platform. like 9-Chan?

538
00:21:47.125 --> 00:21:49.016
Forensics is on that.

539
00:21:50.455 --> 00:21:51.983
Got a name
and work address

540
00:21:52.067 --> 00:21:53.920
of a former girlfriend...
Erica Lawrence.

541
00:21:54.004 --> 00:21:55.428
Multiple domestic calls
to her home

542
00:21:55.512 --> 00:21:56.545
when they were together.

543
00:21:56.629 --> 00:21:58.185
Grey wants us
to interview her.

544
00:21:58.269 --> 00:21:59.699
Right.

545
00:22:01.576 --> 00:22:03.527
I think that's her.

546
00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:06.067
Yeah.

547
00:22:06.151 --> 00:22:07.699
That should be her.

548
00:22:08.676 --> 00:22:09.705
Ms. Lawrence?

549
00:22:09.790 --> 00:22:10.911
Yes?

550
00:22:10.995 --> 00:22:13.568
I'm Detective Lopez.
This is Officer Nolan.

551
00:22:13.652 --> 00:22:16.324
Can you tell us the last time
you saw Marvin Reynolds?

552
00:22:16.442 --> 00:22:17.760
What'd he do?

553
00:22:17.844 --> 00:22:19.717
Shot at us.
for starters.

554
00:22:19.801 --> 00:22:20.967
Have you seen him?

555
00:22:21.051 --> 00:22:23.012
Not since last month.

556
00:22:23.757 --> 00:22:27.016
I started dating someone.
and he found out.

557
00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:28.714
I was so careful
about posting anything.

558
00:22:28.798 --> 00:22:29.998
but somehow. he knew.

559
00:22:30.082 --> 00:22:31.692
What happened?

560
00:22:32.392 --> 00:22:34.051
He came over drunk.

561
00:22:34.238 --> 00:22:37.012
He insisted on playing
Russian Roulette.

562
00:22:37.119 --> 00:22:40.039
He said that
if I deserved to live. that...

563
00:22:40.123 --> 00:22:41.950
fate would save me.

564
00:22:42.152 --> 00:22:43.772
H-He pulled the trigger
three times

565
00:22:43.856 --> 00:22:45.731
before my brother came
and scared him off.

566
00:22:45.815 --> 00:22:47.497
I'm so sorry.

567
00:22:47.637 --> 00:22:50.174
And you didn't file
a restraining order?

568
00:22:50.258 --> 00:22:52.231
I was too scared.

569
00:22:52.886 --> 00:22:55.153
I just want him
to forget I exist.

570
00:22:55.477 --> 00:22:57.341
But now. do y...

571
00:22:57.479 --> 00:22:59.567
Do you think that
he would come for me?

572
00:23:00.003 --> 00:23:01.272
We won't let him.

573
00:23:01.356 --> 00:23:03.156
I'll have a unit come
take you to the station

574
00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:04.576
and wait
until we catch him.

575
00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:05.794
Is there anything
you can tell us

576
00:23:05.878 --> 00:23:07.333
that might help us do that?

577
00:23:07.524 --> 00:23:09.015
Um...

578
00:23:09.099 --> 00:23:11.800
He used to boast
that he had weapons

579
00:23:11.884 --> 00:23:13.106
stashed all over the city.

580
00:23:13.190 --> 00:23:14.629
but he never said where.

581
00:23:14.713 --> 00:23:16.544
What was he gonna
use them for?

582
00:23:16.628 --> 00:23:18.272
Killing people.

583
00:23:18.356 --> 00:23:21.825
But I-I don't know
who. exactly.

584
00:23:21.981 --> 00:23:23.202
He wasn't always like this.

585
00:23:23.286 --> 00:23:26.554
When I first met him.
he was intense and a bit quiet.

586
00:23:26.638 --> 00:23:27.947
but he wasn't radicalized.

587
00:23:28.031 --> 00:23:29.210
Well. what changed?

588
00:23:29.294 --> 00:23:32.582
He met this guy online...
Cooper.

589
00:23:32.666 --> 00:23:35.577
He's the one who pulled him
into the Sovereign Citizens.

590
00:23:35.661 --> 00:23:37.807
Any idea where
we can find Cooper?

591
00:23:37.891 --> 00:23:40.090
You know. you'd think
after the seventh time

592
00:23:40.174 --> 00:23:42.091
this guy posted about
overthrowing the government.

593
00:23:42.175 --> 00:23:43.374
someone might have
called us.

594
00:23:43.458 --> 00:23:46.864
Yeah. it's free speech.
so there's not much we can do.

595
00:23:46.948 --> 00:23:48.446
Donovan call you back?

596
00:23:48.530 --> 00:23:49.546
Nope.

597
00:23:49.630 --> 00:23:51.187
Look. I know
you don't want to put Lila

598
00:23:51.271 --> 00:23:52.718
through any more of this
custody stuff.

599
00:23:52.802 --> 00:23:54.365
but you're not the one
who's doing this.

600
00:23:54.449 --> 00:23:55.601
You know that. right?

601
00:23:55.685 --> 00:23:56.741
He is.

602
00:23:56.825 --> 00:23:58.389
He's the one who decided
to move.

603
00:23:59.541 --> 00:24:01.200
Yeah.

604
00:24:01.331 --> 00:24:02.935
But?

605
00:24:03.372 --> 00:24:06.131
I-I mean. who am I
to say that he can't?

606
00:24:06.286 --> 00:24:08.680
E-Especially after
everything that I did.

607
00:24:10.029 --> 00:24:11.467
Okay. you know what?

608
00:24:11.553 --> 00:24:12.664
Maybe I'm wrong.

609
00:24:12.748 --> 00:24:15.132
and maybe I'm bringing
my own experience into this.

610
00:24:15.216 --> 00:24:18.005
but... I still think
you're punishing yourself.

611
00:24:18.089 --> 00:24:20.216
Yeah. like. y-y-you got this
narrative going right now

612
00:24:20.300 --> 00:24:23.437
where he's the saint
and you're some screw-up.

613
00:24:23.521 --> 00:24:24.664
And you know what?
I-I don't know.

614
00:24:24.748 --> 00:24:27.222
I wasn't there.
a-and maybe you were terrible.

615
00:24:27.306 --> 00:24:29.937
But right now.
he's trying to take your kid.

616
00:24:30.021 --> 00:24:31.296
and you're just
letting him do it

617
00:24:31.380 --> 00:24:32.743
because you're so eaten up
with guilt.

618
00:24:32.827 --> 00:24:34.263
Like...

619
00:24:38.556 --> 00:24:40.902
Cooper Sanford?
I'm Detective Lopez.

620
00:24:40.986 --> 00:24:42.064
This is Officer Nolan.

621
00:24:42.148 --> 00:24:43.414
We're looking
for a friend of yours...

622
00:24:43.498 --> 00:24:44.768
Marvin Reynolds.

623
00:24:44.852 --> 00:24:46.075
Doesn't ring a bell.

624
00:24:46.159 --> 00:24:47.464
See. now.
that's a dumb thing to say.

625
00:24:47.548 --> 00:24:48.815
because clearly. it does.

626
00:24:48.899 --> 00:24:50.785
We heard that you sold him
thousands of dollars' worth

627
00:24:50.869 --> 00:24:52.332
of Sovereign Citizen kits.

628
00:24:53.857 --> 00:24:56.167
- And who told you that?
- We're not telling you that.

629
00:24:56.251 --> 00:24:57.950
Yeah. probably
his bitch of a girlfriend.

630
00:24:58.034 --> 00:24:59.386
He dumped her and moved on.

631
00:24:59.470 --> 00:25:01.273
Can't believe anything
that she says.

632
00:25:01.357 --> 00:25:02.967
So you do know him.

633
00:25:03.626 --> 00:25:05.856
I'm gonna need to see
your delegation of authority.

634
00:25:05.940 --> 00:25:07.266
It's right here.

635
00:25:07.350 --> 00:25:09.008
When was the last time you were
in contact with Marvin?

636
00:25:09.092 --> 00:25:11.436
I don't need to answer
any of your questions.

637
00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:13.439
I'm not a citizen
of your corporation.

638
00:25:13.523 --> 00:25:14.470
My corporation?

639
00:25:14.554 --> 00:25:15.827
In 1871.

640
00:25:15.911 --> 00:25:18.057
the United States
stopped being a country

641
00:25:18.141 --> 00:25:19.655
and started being a corporation.

642
00:25:19.739 --> 00:25:21.647
None of the laws passed
since then in any...

643
00:25:21.731 --> 00:25:24.498
Enough of the
Sovereign Citizen crap!

644
00:25:24.582 --> 00:25:26.506
You need to educate yourself!

645
00:25:26.590 --> 00:25:30.199
This "government" that you serve
sells us all into slavery!

646
00:25:30.283 --> 00:25:32.463
Marvin is planning
a terrorist act.

647
00:25:32.547 --> 00:25:34.265
Do you understand that?

648
00:25:34.349 --> 00:25:35.770
If you have
any knowledge of it.

649
00:25:35.854 --> 00:25:37.119
you're an accessory
after the fact.

650
00:25:37.203 --> 00:25:39.600
whether you believe in the law
or not.

651
00:25:39.684 --> 00:25:41.747
I'm not scared of you!

652
00:25:41.879 --> 00:25:45.535
<i>Flat Worms'
"Surreal New Year" plays...</i>

653
00:25:45.777 --> 00:25:47.387
Whoa. whoa. whoa.

654
00:25:48.432 --> 00:25:49.742
I'm gonna cut him off.

655
00:25:49.826 --> 00:25:51.723
<i>♪ Establishing bricks</i>

656
00:25:54.697 --> 00:25:56.302
Clear it out. Go.
Move out.

657
00:25:56.386 --> 00:25:58.398
<i>♪ ...in your hands</i>

658
00:26:00.567 --> 00:26:01.936
Get out!

659
00:26:13.954 --> 00:26:15.462
Let's try this again.

660
00:26:15.546 --> 00:26:17.671
Where's your friend?
What's he got planned?

661
00:26:17.755 --> 00:26:20.418
I do not recognize
your authority.

662
00:26:20.502 --> 00:26:22.338
I do not answer questions.

663
00:26:22.422 --> 00:26:24.253
You will tell me.
or a lot of people will die.

664
00:26:24.337 --> 00:26:25.994
I do not recognize
your authority!

665
00:26:26.078 --> 00:26:28.402
I do not answer questions!

666
00:26:28.486 --> 00:26:30.021
I could change that.

667
00:26:30.126 --> 00:26:31.043
Aah!
Come on!

668
00:26:31.127 --> 00:26:32.435
What are you doing?

669
00:26:32.519 --> 00:26:33.828
I need a lawyer!

670
00:26:33.912 --> 00:26:35.351
See. all these guys
embrace the legal system

671
00:26:35.435 --> 00:26:36.309
when it serves them!

672
00:26:36.393 --> 00:26:37.484
You need to stop now.
Angela.

673
00:26:37.568 --> 00:26:38.719
Out of my way!

674
00:26:38.803 --> 00:26:40.211
Take a step back.

675
00:26:40.295 --> 00:26:41.357
I outrank you.

676
00:26:41.441 --> 00:26:43.755
Take a step back. ma'am.

677
00:26:44.870 --> 00:26:46.481
Aah.

678
00:26:48.797 --> 00:26:50.498
She was trying to hurt me.

679
00:26:50.582 --> 00:26:52.716
No. She was trying to
scare you.

680
00:26:52.800 --> 00:26:55.054
Now. I could charge you
right now with assault...

681
00:26:55.138 --> 00:26:57.996
Yeah. and I could file
a complaint for abuse.

682
00:26:58.080 --> 00:26:59.912
That is a stretch.

683
00:26:59.996 --> 00:27:01.524
Look. I am willing to
uncuff you right now.

684
00:27:01.608 --> 00:27:03.748
We can put this whole thing
in both our rearview mirrors.

685
00:27:03.832 --> 00:27:07.327
but only if you tell me
what Marvin was planning.

686
00:27:07.411 --> 00:27:09.233
Now. believe this...

687
00:27:09.317 --> 00:27:11.864
The detective
was telling the truth.

688
00:27:12.739 --> 00:27:14.658
If Marvin hurts someone
and you're withholding evidence.

689
00:27:14.742 --> 00:27:16.095
you will be charged
right alongside of him.

690
00:27:16.179 --> 00:27:17.872
And good luck
telling the prison guards

691
00:27:17.956 --> 00:27:19.741
you don't believe in
their authority.

692
00:27:24.511 --> 00:27:25.924
I don't know
where Marvin is.

693
00:27:26.008 --> 00:27:28.250
He called me
about an hour ago.

694
00:27:28.334 --> 00:27:31.756
He asked me to meet him.
bring my guns.

695
00:27:33.412 --> 00:27:36.483
I told him I was all talk
and that he was on his own.

696
00:27:36.699 --> 00:27:39.225
What did he say
he needed the guns for?

697
00:27:39.501 --> 00:27:41.741
He just said
it was go time.

698
00:27:42.560 --> 00:27:45.722
And that I'd probably
never see him again.

699
00:27:51.386 --> 00:27:52.559
Maybe I should
just let it go.

700
00:27:52.643 --> 00:27:54.270
but that house
was my childhood home.

701
00:27:54.354 --> 00:27:55.828
I don't want to
tear it down.

702
00:27:55.912 --> 00:27:57.169
I want another family
to live there

703
00:27:57.253 --> 00:27:58.544
and make happy memories.

704
00:27:58.628 --> 00:27:59.778
Of course.

705
00:27:59.862 --> 00:28:02.325
I moved out 10 years ago.
and when I think of home.

706
00:28:02.409 --> 00:28:04.182
I still think of
my parents' house.

707
00:28:05.584 --> 00:28:07.235
What's wrong?

708
00:28:08.088 --> 00:28:09.510
Tim?

709
00:28:11.841 --> 00:28:14.387
Look. I know you don't feel
the same way I do.

710
00:28:14.471 --> 00:28:16.887
but our childhood
wasn't all bad.

711
00:28:16.971 --> 00:28:18.369
Stop.

712
00:28:18.581 --> 00:28:19.852
Alright?

713
00:28:19.936 --> 00:28:22.481
Are you really getting nostalgic
over that place?

714
00:28:22.565 --> 00:28:24.422
What... What do you want?
Some other family

715
00:28:24.506 --> 00:28:26.418
to just cuddle up
under the broken plaster

716
00:28:26.502 --> 00:28:28.416
where dad slammed my head
against the wall?

717
00:28:29.181 --> 00:28:30.559
Dad had a lot of demons.

718
00:28:30.643 --> 00:28:32.247
Dad was a monster.

719
00:28:32.331 --> 00:28:33.674
He's changed.

720
00:28:34.120 --> 00:28:35.950
You haven't seen him
in 20 years.

721
00:28:36.034 --> 00:28:37.782
The only thing
that's changed

722
00:28:37.866 --> 00:28:39.293
is that the drinking
caught up with him.

723
00:28:39.377 --> 00:28:40.708
- Okay?
- He can't throw a punch.

724
00:28:40.792 --> 00:28:42.387
but he's the same guy
underneath.

725
00:28:42.471 --> 00:28:45.657
He's not. and you'd know that
if you'd visit the hospice.

726
00:28:45.792 --> 00:28:47.177
Not in a million years.

727
00:28:47.261 --> 00:28:48.794
Wait. hospice?

728
00:28:48.878 --> 00:28:52.103
I had to move him out of
assisted living last month.

729
00:28:53.503 --> 00:28:54.983
Dad's dying.

730
00:29:11.030 --> 00:29:12.286
I know you and Wesley

731
00:29:12.370 --> 00:29:13.809
are going through a lot
right now.

732
00:29:13.893 --> 00:29:14.820
but that's no excuse.

733
00:29:14.904 --> 00:29:16.169
I wasn't actually
going to hurt him.

734
00:29:16.253 --> 00:29:17.910
It doesn't matter.

735
00:29:17.994 --> 00:29:19.912
We can't play "bad cop"
anymore.

736
00:29:19.996 --> 00:29:21.304
We have to rise above
that way of thinking

737
00:29:21.388 --> 00:29:22.604
because it's corrosive.

738
00:29:24.687 --> 00:29:26.222
You're right.
I'm sorry.

739
00:29:26.306 --> 00:29:27.783
Thank you.

740
00:29:28.907 --> 00:29:31.184
Silver Honda...
That could be Marvin's car.

741
00:29:31.268 --> 00:29:33.142
Plate's a match.
That's him.

742
00:29:33.226 --> 00:29:36.185
Control. 7-Adam-15. we have eyes
on Marvin Reynolds' vehicle.

743
00:29:36.277 --> 00:29:37.456
Stand by.

744
00:29:47.371 --> 00:29:49.028
7-Adam-100. 7-Adam-15.

745
00:29:49.112 --> 00:29:51.030
we've cleared the vehicle.
no sign of suspect.

746
00:29:51.114 --> 00:29:52.540
Secure the location
and sit tight

747
00:29:52.624 --> 00:29:53.647
until TID arrives.

748
00:29:53.731 --> 00:29:54.716
Copy that.

749
00:29:54.800 --> 00:29:57.003
Lopez. you see this?

750
00:29:57.353 --> 00:29:58.911
Oil leak.

751
00:29:58.995 --> 00:30:01.610
There was a big vehicle here
parked for some time.

752
00:30:01.694 --> 00:30:03.403
The street cleaners had to
maneuver around it.

753
00:30:03.487 --> 00:30:04.912
Another weapons stash?

754
00:30:04.996 --> 00:30:06.983
So he ditched the Civic
and drove off in an arsenal?

755
00:30:07.067 --> 00:30:08.246
<i>You finally got rid of it.</i>

756
00:30:08.330 --> 00:30:09.117
Rid of what?

757
00:30:09.201 --> 00:30:10.417
That van.

758
00:30:10.540 --> 00:30:12.502
I must've called a hundred times
trying to get it towed.

759
00:30:12.586 --> 00:30:15.634
Well. then. uh. you must
remember some details about it?

760
00:30:15.718 --> 00:30:16.977
Yeah.

761
00:30:19.555 --> 00:30:22.065
Hey. I-I know a great
bereavement counselor.

762
00:30:22.149 --> 00:30:23.677
if you need someone
to talk to.

763
00:30:23.761 --> 00:30:26.047
I have someone. Thanks.

764
00:30:26.370 --> 00:30:27.869
You know. therapy's really
helped me come to terms

765
00:30:27.953 --> 00:30:30.985
with everything that happened
to us when we were kids.

766
00:30:31.857 --> 00:30:33.594
It could help you. too.

767
00:30:33.703 --> 00:30:35.268
I'm good.

768
00:30:35.352 --> 00:30:37.705
You really don't think
you carry some trauma

769
00:30:37.789 --> 00:30:39.142
from what
he put you through?

770
00:30:39.226 --> 00:30:40.449
When you were 7 years old.

771
00:30:40.533 --> 00:30:42.060
he dropped you in Griffith Park
with a compass

772
00:30:42.144 --> 00:30:43.019
and made you
find your way home.

773
00:30:43.103 --> 00:30:44.369
Which I did.

774
00:30:44.453 --> 00:30:45.850
A Tim Test.

775
00:30:45.934 --> 00:30:47.010
A what?

776
00:30:47.094 --> 00:30:48.356
Nothing. Um...

777
00:30:49.580 --> 00:30:52.925
Oh. We got a hit on the van
that Nolan and Lopez I.D.'d.

778
00:30:53.009 --> 00:30:55.362
It's racked up
hundreds of dollars in fines.

779
00:30:55.446 --> 00:30:56.292
Parking tickets?

780
00:30:56.376 --> 00:30:57.433
And tolls.

781
00:30:57.517 --> 00:30:58.600
Where are they clustered?

782
00:30:58.684 --> 00:31:00.316
Uh. they're centered around
the Port of Los Angeles.

783
00:31:00.400 --> 00:31:01.566
Didn't the intel report
state

784
00:31:01.650 --> 00:31:02.746
that Marvin used to work
down there?

785
00:31:02.830 --> 00:31:03.902
Drove a forklift
or something?

786
00:31:03.986 --> 00:31:05.147
Yeah. but he was fired
two years ago.

787
00:31:05.231 --> 00:31:06.915
Why would he
be visiting now?

788
00:31:07.258 --> 00:31:08.908
I'll send some units.

789
00:31:11.262 --> 00:31:13.267
Air Three has eyes
on suspect vehicle.

790
00:31:13.351 --> 00:31:15.922
Northeast corner of lot A.
just off Front Street.

791
00:31:16.006 --> 00:31:17.357
I'm gonna orbit.

792
00:31:17.442 --> 00:31:19.772
Control. 7-Adam-15.
show us responding.

793
00:31:21.470 --> 00:31:24.351
Air Three. 7-Adam-07.
arriving at location.

794
00:31:24.435 --> 00:31:26.111
Stand by.

795
00:31:31.585 --> 00:31:34.021
Air Three. 7-Adam-07.
any movement?

796
00:31:35.677 --> 00:31:39.108
7-Adam-07. I see no movement
in suspect vehicle.

797
00:31:43.728 --> 00:31:47.036
Aaron. relax
and follow my lead.

798
00:32:00.354 --> 00:32:01.634
Front seat clear.

799
00:32:15.275 --> 00:32:16.708
Clear.

800
00:32:18.267 --> 00:32:21.400
Air Three. 7-Adam-07.
no sign of suspect.

801
00:32:21.485 --> 00:32:23.424
but he is
clearly well-armed.

802
00:32:23.508 --> 00:32:26.732
Marvin just posted something
to social media.

803
00:32:26.816 --> 00:32:30.683
History is gonna remember
this day as Sovereigns' Day.

804
00:32:30.767 --> 00:32:31.888
I'm about to light the spark

805
00:32:31.972 --> 00:32:33.707
that's gonna ignite
the revolution.

806
00:32:33.791 --> 00:32:36.153
Maybe we can spot something
that gives away his location.

807
00:32:36.237 --> 00:32:37.411
It's hard to tell.

808
00:32:37.495 --> 00:32:39.416
And who knows
when he recorded that.

809
00:32:40.712 --> 00:32:42.008
I mean. why here?

810
00:32:42.092 --> 00:32:44.403
Uh. there are dozens of targets
at the port.

811
00:32:44.487 --> 00:32:46.754
from the cruise ship terminal
to the port itself.

812
00:32:46.838 --> 00:32:48.952
Yeah. or maybe he's here to kill
the boss that fired him

813
00:32:49.036 --> 00:32:50.731
and pretend
it's for some great cause.

814
00:32:53.466 --> 00:32:54.997
We're taking fire!
We need to back off!

815
00:32:55.081 --> 00:32:57.107
Do you have a location
on the shooter?

816
00:32:57.191 --> 00:32:58.731
Negative. negative.

817
00:32:59.313 --> 00:33:00.659
Where the hell is he?

818
00:33:05.557 --> 00:33:07.107
Air Three.
suspect heading north

819
00:33:07.191 --> 00:33:09.185
along the water.
armed with a long gun.

820
00:33:09.269 --> 00:33:11.043
We're climbing to a safe
altitude. then I'll swing back.

821
00:33:11.127 --> 00:33:13.083
Police. stop!

822
00:33:23.363 --> 00:33:26.144
Control. 7-Adam-07.
alert Long Beach Police.

823
00:33:26.228 --> 00:33:28.013
we are taking fire.

824
00:33:28.104 --> 00:33:31.111
Moving to channel 13
for mutual aid.

825
00:33:31.550 --> 00:33:32.987
Secure that weapon.

826
00:33:44.808 --> 00:33:46.505
We have to stop him before
he gets on that ship.

827
00:34:08.714 --> 00:34:10.245
Clear!

828
00:34:11.414 --> 00:34:14.291
Move! Clear!
Everyone. clear!

829
00:34:14.375 --> 00:34:15.341
What do you got?

830
00:34:15.425 --> 00:34:17.059
Single shooter we've been
tracking since L.A.

831
00:34:17.143 --> 00:34:19.167
- Where is he?
- Somewhere on that boat.

832
00:34:20.944 --> 00:34:23.313
Stay here
in case he doubles back.

833
00:34:23.510 --> 00:34:25.454
Move. move. move!
Come. come.

834
00:34:28.174 --> 00:34:29.784
We should split up.

835
00:34:38.233 --> 00:34:40.061
Covering.

836
00:34:41.333 --> 00:34:42.680
Clear. Clear.

837
00:34:44.209 --> 00:34:45.492
Clear.

838
00:34:48.306 --> 00:34:49.594
Clear.

839
00:34:51.794 --> 00:34:53.056
Holding.

840
00:34:54.517 --> 00:34:56.033
Clear.

841
00:34:59.540 --> 00:35:00.889
Holding.

842
00:35:02.227 --> 00:35:03.544
Go.

843
00:35:04.508 --> 00:35:06.164
Oh.
It's okay.

844
00:35:06.248 --> 00:35:07.111
Stay calm.

845
00:35:07.195 --> 00:35:08.666
Keep going going this way.
exit the ship.

846
00:35:08.750 --> 00:35:10.441
There's other officers
waiting outside.

847
00:35:18.295 --> 00:35:19.743
Exit out that door.

848
00:35:19.827 --> 00:35:21.618
It's a straight shot outside.
okay?

849
00:35:21.702 --> 00:35:23.428
It's clear.
We just came from that way.

850
00:35:23.512 --> 00:35:24.774
Go.

851
00:35:30.656 --> 00:35:31.962
It's all clear.

852
00:35:36.547 --> 00:35:38.375
Clear.

853
00:35:39.696 --> 00:35:40.742
Clear.

854
00:35:41.745 --> 00:35:42.961
Lopez.

855
00:35:50.934 --> 00:35:52.637
Don't move!
It's okay.

856
00:35:52.903 --> 00:35:53.932
Whoa.
You're safe. you're safe.

857
00:35:54.016 --> 00:35:55.104
Please.
Please get me out of here.

858
00:35:55.188 --> 00:35:55.962
Please get me out of here.

859
00:35:56.046 --> 00:35:57.313
You have to let him go
first.

860
00:35:57.397 --> 00:35:59.045
Okay. I-I'm sorry.
That's alright.

861
00:35:59.704 --> 00:36:00.915
What is that?

862
00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:02.932
You stay here.
You'll be safe. alright?

863
00:36:03.016 --> 00:36:03.998
Please don't leave me!

864
00:36:04.082 --> 00:36:05.593
Just lock the door
behind us.

865
00:36:10.524 --> 00:36:12.054
Hey!

866
00:37:23.348 --> 00:37:24.749
Drop it!

867
00:37:43.069 --> 00:37:45.086
- You're right.
- About what?

868
00:37:45.170 --> 00:37:46.733
I need to fight for Lila.

869
00:37:46.817 --> 00:37:48.514
Even if I lose.
she needs to know

870
00:37:48.598 --> 00:37:49.834
that I would do anything
for her.

871
00:37:49.918 --> 00:37:51.137
You're not gonna lose.

872
00:37:54.557 --> 00:37:56.330
Yeah. I'm not so sure.

873
00:37:56.414 --> 00:38:00.270
I mean. my lawyer is
a lovely person but...

874
00:38:00.394 --> 00:38:02.311
Actually. that might be
the issue.

875
00:38:02.395 --> 00:38:04.836
She's too nice
to be a divorce lawyer.

876
00:38:04.920 --> 00:38:07.274
Well. then hire
someone better... or worse.

877
00:38:07.358 --> 00:38:08.836
Better lawyer.
worse person.

878
00:38:08.920 --> 00:38:11.187
Me and whose paycheck?

879
00:38:11.271 --> 00:38:12.405
Use my lawyer.

880
00:38:12.489 --> 00:38:15.661
She is a shark.
and she owes me one.

881
00:38:15.792 --> 00:38:18.147
The press around my trial
tripled her business.

882
00:38:18.231 --> 00:38:20.019
She'll give you
the friends and family discount.

883
00:38:20.103 --> 00:38:21.661
I'll send you the details.

884
00:38:22.226 --> 00:38:24.097
- Thanks.
- Happy to help.

885
00:38:24.370 --> 00:38:25.984
<i>Chance Peña's "Anxiety
& Mixed Emotions" plays...</i>

886
00:38:26.068 --> 00:38:26.985
- Hey.
- Hm?

887
00:38:27.069 --> 00:38:27.724
Where's Genny?

888
00:38:27.808 --> 00:38:30.299
Oh. she is
calling your nephews.

889
00:38:30.383 --> 00:38:33.613
Um. Tim. listen. uh...

890
00:38:34.624 --> 00:38:36.516
Your sister needs you.

891
00:38:36.600 --> 00:38:39.910
Lucy... I-I realize
that I'm overstepping here.

892
00:38:39.994 --> 00:38:41.721
but just hear me out.

893
00:38:41.886 --> 00:38:43.741
It's clear that
you got the worst of it

894
00:38:43.825 --> 00:38:44.566
with your father.

895
00:38:44.650 --> 00:38:46.371
but she lived through it
with you.

896
00:38:46.455 --> 00:38:50.098
Instead of arguing about
how bad your dad was or wasn't.

897
00:38:50.182 --> 00:38:54.697
maybe as... as children
of abuse.

898
00:38:55.213 --> 00:38:57.929
you would be better off
just supporting each other.

899
00:38:58.013 --> 00:39:00.199
Hey.
You ready to go?

900
00:39:00.283 --> 00:39:01.932
Yeah.

901
00:39:02.113 --> 00:39:04.463
Look. I'm really sorry
about today.

902
00:39:05.271 --> 00:39:06.846
I should've listened more.

903
00:39:07.502 --> 00:39:08.741
I agree.

904
00:39:08.825 --> 00:39:09.949
<i>♪ Tell me that I'm worth it</i>

905
00:39:10.033 --> 00:39:12.402
But thanks for saying it.
That means a lot.

906
00:39:12.486 --> 00:39:14.775
I'm still not going to
see him.

907
00:39:15.030 --> 00:39:17.121
<i>♪ ...I think about</i>

908
00:39:17.205 --> 00:39:20.105
Oh. uh. Nolan.
this is my sister Genny.

909
00:39:20.189 --> 00:39:21.760
Oh! Nice to finally meet you
in person.

910
00:39:21.844 --> 00:39:24.018
I'm so grateful you're willing
to help out with dad's house.

911
00:39:24.102 --> 00:39:25.309
Ah. it's my pleasure.

912
00:39:25.393 --> 00:39:26.645
You know. if you're free
this weekend.

913
00:39:26.729 --> 00:39:28.873
maybe we could go by the place.
see what needs to be done.

914
00:39:28.957 --> 00:39:30.092
and you could give us
an estimate.

915
00:39:30.176 --> 00:39:31.510
Did you just say "we"?

916
00:39:32.178 --> 00:39:33.262
As in you're gonna help?

917
00:39:33.346 --> 00:39:36.446
Well. I checked out some comps
in the neighborhood.

918
00:39:36.530 --> 00:39:38.844
and we can get a million
for that place. easy.

919
00:39:38.928 --> 00:39:41.276
Plus. it shouldn't all
fall on you.

920
00:39:42.098 --> 00:39:43.520
Thanks.

921
00:39:43.604 --> 00:39:45.401
I'll see you both
Saturday.

922
00:39:46.432 --> 00:39:47.739
Nolan.

923
00:39:47.823 --> 00:39:49.378
One second.
Come here.

924
00:39:50.330 --> 00:39:53.855
Hey. can I have
everyone's attention. please?

925
00:39:54.066 --> 00:39:56.058
<i>♪ ...what this world
has for me ♪</i>

926
00:39:56.142 --> 00:39:58.176
<i>♪ Do it all on my own</i>

927
00:39:58.260 --> 00:40:01.659
I would like to formally give
my endorsement for union rep

928
00:40:01.743 --> 00:40:05.823
to a man who has the backs of
every officer in this station...

929
00:40:05.907 --> 00:40:07.411
<i>♪ All on my own</i>

930
00:40:07.495 --> 00:40:08.666
John Nolan.

931
00:40:08.816 --> 00:40:10.695
Et tu. Bradford?

932
00:40:10.863 --> 00:40:13.067
Alright. Nolan.
Good endorsement.

933
00:40:13.151 --> 00:40:14.500
Yeah!

934
00:40:15.831 --> 00:40:18.377
<i>♪ Do it all on my own</i>

935
00:40:18.461 --> 00:40:20.445
Thank you. guys.
Thank you very much.

936
00:40:20.529 --> 00:40:22.484
- Good job. man.
- Great job.

937
00:40:22.568 --> 00:40:23.736
Thank you.
Don't forget to vote.

938
00:40:23.820 --> 00:40:24.973
Don't forget to vote at all.

939
00:40:25.057 --> 00:40:26.101
Thank you.

940
00:40:28.974 --> 00:40:31.893
<i>♪ Ooh. ooh</i>

941
00:40:31.977 --> 00:40:33.982
Is that the solution
to all your problems?

942
00:40:34.066 --> 00:40:35.102
I hope so.

943
00:40:35.186 --> 00:40:37.430
I just hope it's enough
to make the case against Elijah.

944
00:40:37.514 --> 00:40:39.470
Listen.
about today.

945
00:40:39.554 --> 00:40:40.821
don't be too hard
on yourself.

946
00:40:40.905 --> 00:40:42.907
You've been going through a lot
these past few months.

947
00:40:42.991 --> 00:40:44.997
Not an excuse.
I know better.

948
00:40:45.081 --> 00:40:47.040
I'm just glad you were there
to remind me.

949
00:40:52.033 --> 00:40:53.397
What are you doing here?

950
00:40:54.354 --> 00:40:55.610
I'm doing the right thing.

951
00:40:55.694 --> 00:40:57.922
Sergeant Grey came to me
last week. offered his help.

952
00:40:58.006 --> 00:40:59.352
Today. I finally took it.

953
00:41:01.331 --> 00:41:02.523
You told him everything?

954
00:41:02.607 --> 00:41:04.202
Everything.

955
00:41:04.376 --> 00:41:06.430
From the first time I approached
Elijah until today.

956
00:41:06.514 --> 00:41:08.128
How the hell
does that help us?

957
00:41:08.212 --> 00:41:09.800
Because Sergeant Grey
accepted my offer

958
00:41:09.884 --> 00:41:11.467
to be a cooperating witness.

959
00:41:11.633 --> 00:41:12.970
No. you're not doing that.

960
00:41:13.054 --> 00:41:14.655
That will get you
killed.

961
00:41:15.423 --> 00:41:16.852
I've been working all day.

962
00:41:16.936 --> 00:41:18.258
and I think
with a little more digging.

963
00:41:18.342 --> 00:41:20.332
we can hang a RICO case
on Elijah.

964
00:41:20.416 --> 00:41:22.073
But any good lawyer
will swat that away.

965
00:41:22.157 --> 00:41:24.821
He will never see
a jail cell.

966
00:41:24.905 --> 00:41:26.866
Well. you're not
becoming a C.I.

967
00:41:27.839 --> 00:41:29.727
What about attorney-client
privilege?

968
00:41:29.811 --> 00:41:31.405
That could get you
disbarred.

969
00:41:32.096 --> 00:41:33.725
Some things are hard to do.

970
00:41:34.700 --> 00:41:36.436
Some things are scary.

971
00:41:36.529 --> 00:41:40.272
This is both.
but it's something I have to do.

972
00:41:40.496 --> 00:41:43.507
It's not for me. it's for you.
And Jack.

973
00:41:44.385 --> 00:41:46.707
So. look. Angela.
I've already got calls in

974
00:41:46.791 --> 00:41:49.827
to the State's Attorney General
and District Attorney.

975
00:41:50.055 --> 00:41:51.672
They already got a game plan.

976
00:41:51.756 --> 00:41:55.459
and I will personally oversee
how Wesley is utilized.

977
00:41:55.543 --> 00:41:57.181
I promise.

978
00:41:57.265 --> 00:42:00.193
I will do everything humanly
possible to keep him safe.

979
00:42:02.991 --> 00:42:05.036
I need you to tell me
this is okay.

980
00:42:05.192 --> 00:42:07.100
I won't do it
without your support.

981
00:42:11.248 --> 00:42:12.999
We can't screw this up.

982
00:42:14.437 --> 00:42:16.313
Not a single mistake.

983
00:42:16.397 --> 00:42:17.963
Not one.

984
00:42:18.063 --> 00:42:19.234
We won't.

985
00:42:19.382 --> 00:42:20.704
I promise you.

986
00:42:20.788 --> 00:42:23.009
<font color=#ffc30f>Sync corrections</font> by <font color=#00FF00>srjanapala</font>

987
00:42:24.305 --> 00:43:24.167
